Factor-sweep paired t-tests, spectral+content vs each NF-MCD variant, per cell (5 seeds).
Benjamini-Hochberg FDR correction applied across 50 cells, separately per NF-MCD variant.

=== spectral+content vs nfmcd_alpha_fixed ===
  cells where spectral+content has higher mean (nominal): 46/50
  of those, significant at raw p<0.05: 42/50
  of those, significant after BH correction (q<0.05): 41/50
  cells where nfmcd_alpha_fixed has higher mean (nominal): 4/50
  of those, significant after BH correction (q<0.05): 0/50

=== spectral+content vs nfmcd_adaptive ===
  cells where spectral+content has higher mean (nominal): 46/50
  of those, significant at raw p<0.05: 42/50
  of those, significant after BH correction (q<0.05): 39/50
  cells where nfmcd_adaptive has higher mean (nominal): 4/50
  of those, significant after BH correction (q<0.05): 0/50

Per-regime breakdown (spectral+content vs adaptive-alpha NF-MCD, the paper's default):
  strong_struct_weak_content: 14/25 cells significant (BH q<0.05) in favor of spectral+content
  weak_struct_strong_content: 25/25 cells significant (BH q<0.05) in favor of spectral+content